# The PostgreSQL patch catalog is checksum-verified byte-for-byte by
# apply-patches.sh and hotel-desktop/src-tauri/src/postgres/patches.rs, which
# hash the raw file bytes with no newline normalization. A CRLF checkout on
# Windows (core.autocrlf=true) therefore fails every manifest checksum and the
# runner aborts the whole catalog, leaving databases stuck on the baseline.
# Pin every SQL file and the manifest to LF so the hashes match everywhere.
*.sql text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf
